// Package pyc reproduces the CPython 3.14 behaviours the builder output depends on: int and float floor division,
// round(), struct '<f', json.dumps/json.loads, bytes.decode('utf-8', 'replace') and NFKD -> ascii-ignore.
// The reference is the frozen oracle python.exe; testdata/pyc holds vectors generated by gen/gen_pyc_vectors.py.
//
// Float code here never fuses operations (GOAMD64=v1 has no FMA); callers porting expressions like
// t0 + b*DT - 1 must keep Python's evaluation order and wrap each product in float64() to forbid fusion.
package pyc
